  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "On the surface of a globe, the geography teacher drew 10 parallels and 10 meridians. Into how many areas has the surface of the globe thus been divided?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "81"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "90"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "100"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "110"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "121"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Bands times sectors",
    "body": "A meridian is a half circle from the North Pole to the South Pole. 10 meridians cut the globe like an orange into 10 slices.\n\nA parallel is a circle around the globe at a fixed latitude. 10 parallels cut the globe into 11 horizontal bands.\n\nEach band is cut by the meridians into 10 pieces: $11 \\times 10 = 110$ areas.\n\n**Answer: (D) 110**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Add one line at a time",
    "body": "With the 10 meridians only, there are 10 areas. Each new parallel crosses all 10 slices and splits each into two, adding 10 areas. After 10 parallels: $10 + 10 \\times 10 = 110$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 110**"
   }
  ],
