  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "Francois says: \"On my 60th birthday I got many presents, and I hope to get as many on my 80th. Each of my children has as many children of their own as siblings, and none has grandchildren yet. My age is now equal to the number of all my living descendants.\" How old is Francois?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "62"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "64"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "67"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "70"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "72"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "B",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Descendants form a square",
    "body": "Let Francois have $n$ children. Each child has $n - 1$ siblings, so each child has $n - 1$ children of their own. There are no great-grandchildren.\n\nDescendants: $n + n(n-1) = n^2$.\n\nHis age is a perfect square between 60 and 80 (he has had his 60th birthday but not yet his 80th): only $64 = 8^2$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 64**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Test the choices",
    "body": "The number of descendants $n + n(n-1) = n^2$ must be a perfect square. Among 62, 64, 67, 70, 72 only 64 is a square (8 children, each with 7 children: $8 + 56 = 64$).\n\n**Answer: (B) 64**"
   }
  ],
