 {
  "id": "kangaroo-ca-2013-g0708-23",
  "bank": "kangaroo",
  "source": {
   "contest": "Canadian Math Kangaroo",
   "paper": "Grade 7-8",
   "year": 2013,
   "number": 23,
   "url": "https://api.mathkangaroo.ca/api/v1/media/2013/2013gr0708e.pdf"
  },
  "grade": "7-8",
  "points": 5,
  "timeMinutes": null,
  "type": "mc",
  "prompt": "Recall that a perfect square is a number that can be represented as a product of two equal factors, for example $25 = 5 \\times 5 = 5^2$. A perfect cube is a number that can be represented as a product of three equal factors, for example $8 = 2 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 2^3$. A product of six equal factors can be written as a power, for example $2^6 = 2\\times2\\times2\\times2\\times2\\times2$. Let $S$ be the number of perfect squares among the integers from 1 to $2013^6$. Let $Q$ be the number of perfect cubes among the same integers. Which of the following statements is true?",
  "image": null,
  "choices": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "text": "$S = Q$"
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "text": "$2S = 3Q$"
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "text": "$3S = 2Q$"
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "text": "$S = 2013Q$"
   },
   {
    "key": "E",
    "text": "$S^3 = Q^2$"
   }
  ],
  "answer": "D",
  "acceptedAnswers": null,
  "answerUnit": null,
  "solutions": [
   {
    "title": "Count squares and cubes",
    "body": "The squares $1^2, 2^2, \\dots, k^2$ up to $2013^6 = (2013^3)^2$: there are $S = 2013^3$ of them.\n\nThe cubes $1^3, 2^3, \\dots$ up to $2013^6 = (2013^2)^3$: there are $Q = 2013^2$ of them.\n\nSo $S = 2013^3 = 2013 \\cdot 2013^2 = 2013\\,Q$.\n\n**Answer: (D) $S = 2013Q$**"
   },
   {
    "title": "Small example",
    "body": "Replace 2013 by 2: up to $2^6 = 64$ there are $S = 8$ squares ($1,4,\\dots,64$) and $Q = 4$ cubes ($1, 8, 27, 64$). Then $S = 2Q$, which matches the pattern $S = 2013Q$ with 2013 replaced by 2, and none of the other relations holds ($S^3 = 512 \\ne Q^2 = 16$).\n\n**Answer: (D) $S = 2013Q$**"
   }
  ],
  "topics": [
   "number-theory"
  ],
  "difficulty": 3,
  "duplicateOf": null,
  "reviewNote": null
 },
